The original copyright notices are retained verbatim in every derived
source file. Source files that carry Kyle York's code and were modified
by the fork are marked with a "Co-author: Matthew Schinkel" line inside
the original header block; files byte-identical to the jalv25r9 baseline
are unmodified. The upstream repository publishes no LICENSE file; its
files are redistributed here with their original notices intact.

The pre-built jalv2 compiler binaries under bin/old_versions/
(jalv24q6 .. jalv25r9, all platforms) are redistributed from the jalv2
releases of the same upstream project.

The JAL libraries under demo_lib/ and the samples under demo_sample/
originate from jallib 2.1 (https://github.com/jallib/jallib, ZLIB
license) and the upstream compiler distribution; authorship is stated
in each file's own header, and the same applies to libraries and
samples created for the fork's own test and demo work. The pristine
jallib corpus used by the unit gate is fetched, not vendored
(unit-tests/fetch_jallib.sh, checksum-pinned).

Fork extensions — the ESP32 (Xtensa LX6) and PIC32 (MIPS32) back ends,
the dynamic string heap, pointers, native bit arrays, wide integers, the
shared algorithm kernels, the simulator suites (sims/) and the unit-test
gate (unit-tests/) — are

